P1 — instance-name multiplicity of the optimized module: a reviewable patch
==========================================================================

Status: PROPOSAL, hand-written against 4d3cd186, NOT applied, NOT built.
Worker A. The hunks below are written by reading the two files; line numbers
are approximate — apply by the context lines.

Where the check lives
---------------------
`hierRefineCheck` and `checkedOptimize` are in `Sparkle/IR/RefineCheck.lean`,
`instsKept` / `deinline` in `Sparkle/IR/HierCheck.lean`: compiler-side IR
files (not `Tools/`). So this is a compiler change.

What is needed, and which form gives it
---------------------------------------
Target (a conjunct of `hierCheck` and of `textCheckI`):

    (instNames (checkedOptimize b).body).Nodup

from the run fact `(instNames b.body).Nodup` (`MachineWired`).

* Today: `instsKept m o && instsKept o m` — the instance statements of `o`
  and `m` are the same SET. A repeated instance statement in `o` passes.
  Not enough.
* Form A — exact list: `o.body.filter isInst = m.body.filter isInst`.
  Gives `instNames o.body = instNames m.body` (so nodup transfers), and the
  ORDER of the instances. Rejects any reordering of instance statements.
* Form B — multiset + nodup: `(o.body.filter isInst).Perm (m.body.filter
  isInst)` (decidable via counts) together with nodup of `m`'s names. Gives
  `instNames o.body ~ instNames m.body`, hence nodup. Does not reject
  reorderings.
* Form C — nodup of `o`'s instance names alone:
  `decide (instNamesOf o.body).Nodup`. With the two `instsKept` conjuncts
  already there, `o`'s instance statements are then a duplicate-free (by
  name) list with the same set as `m`'s. It gives the target DIRECTLY, with
  no reference to `m`'s nodup, and rejects only an output that repeats an
  instance name.

For the target, ORDER IS NOT NEEDED and the multiset equality is not needed
either: Form C suffices and rejects least. (Order would matter for
`linkedWF` — P2 — but P2 constrains assignments relative to instances, which
no instance-list equality gives; see docs/parallel/G1-checks.md §6.)
Form A or B would only be wanted if some later proof needs
`instNames o.body = instNames m.body` as lists; none does today.

Measured (integrator's run of Tests/Compiler/ChecksDerivedTest.lean, 27 real
parents): `instNamesNodup(o)` is true on every one, and so is the list
equality P1 — so on the corpus' parents none of A, B, C rejects anything.

Shape of the patch: fall back, never reject
-------------------------------------------
The new test is applied to the candidate BEFORE `hierRefineCheck` sees it:
a candidate with a repeated instance name is replaced by the input module
`m`. `checkedOptimize` keeps its shape `if hierRefineCheck m o' then o' else
m`, so the theorems about an accepted `o'` (`hierRefineCheck_linked`,
`hierRefineCheck_linkedH`, `hierRefineCheck_inputs`,
`hierRefineCheck_inst_iff`) are untouched; only the four lemmas that spell
the candidate out change one term (listed below). No source is rejected: the
worst case is the unoptimised module `m`, which is what `checkedOptimize`
already returns when the check fails.

--- a/Sparkle/IR/HierCheck.lean
+++ b/Sparkle/IR/HierCheck.lean
@@ (after `def instsKept`, before `def connRefs`)
     | _ => true

+/-- The instance names of a body, in order. -/
+def instNamesOf (body : List Stmt) : List String :=
+  body.filterMap fun st =>
+    match st with
+    | .inst _ iname _ => some iname
+    | _ => none
+
+/-- The candidate `o` when its instance names are pairwise distinct, else
+the input module `m`: an optimizer output that repeats an instance name is
+not shipped. -/
+def keepNodup (m o : Module) : Module :=
+  if decide (instNamesOf o.body).Nodup then o else m
+
+theorem keepNodup_nodup {m : Module} (o : Module)
+    (hm : (instNamesOf m.body).Nodup) : (instNamesOf (keepNodup m o).body).Nodup := by
+  unfold keepNodup
+  split
+  · rename_i h
+    exact of_decide_eq_true h
+  · exact hm
+
 /-- The wires the instance statements connect. -/
 def connRefs (body : List Stmt) : List String :=

--- a/Sparkle/IR/RefineCheck.lean
+++ b/Sparkle/IR/RefineCheck.lean
@@ def checkedOptimize (m : Module) : Module :=
   -- instances: checked on the extracted interface, where that check binds
   else if RefineCheck.hierBinds m then
-    let o' := Sparkle.IR.HierCheck.deinline m o
+    -- (a candidate that repeats an instance name is replaced by `m`)
+    let o' := Sparkle.IR.HierCheck.keepNodup m (Sparkle.IR.HierCheck.deinline m o)
     if RefineCheck.hierRefineCheck m o' then o' else m
   else o

